body:
Source: GitHub issue #1062 (bug, security, false-green). Re-verified on main @ b2b5c6ea: `packages/core/lib/railpath.mjs:26-30` —

    if (existsSync(abs)) {
      resolved = realpathOr(abs);
    } else {
      resolved = join(realpathOr(dirname(abs)), basename(abs));
    }

When the target is missing only ONE parent level is realpath'd. If that parent is missing too, `realpathSync` throws, `realpathOr` returns the lexical string, and a symlink further up is never resolved — although the function's own JSDoc (`:19-20`) promises "the deepest existing ancestor". Repro, fixture `test/` exists, `src/alias -> ../test`, `test/newdir` absent:

    resolveRailPath('src/alias/x.test.mjs', root)        -> 'test/x.test.mjs'              (correct)
    resolveRailPath('src/alias/newdir/x.test.mjs', root) -> 'src/alias/newdir/x.test.mjs'  (wrong; must be 'test/newdir/x.test.mjs')

Both importers add this value to the candidate set they glob-match against the frozen rails, so the miss is a false ALLOW at the hook decision: `plugins/adlc-pi/lib/rails-checker.mjs:89` — `checkStructuredWrite('src/alias/newdir/x.test.mjs', { rails: ['test/**'] }, root).decision` is `'allow'`; `plugins/adlc-opencode/rails-checker.mjs:616` — `checkRail({ filePath: 'aliasdir/newdir/new.mjs', tool: 'write', root, env })` with rail `locked/**` and `aliasdir -> locked` is `'allow'`, while `'aliasdir/new.mjs'` is `'deny'`. Only a NEW file in a NOT-YET-EXISTING subdirectory reached through a symlinked directory is affected.

CORE FREEZE: this change is authorized. CONVENTIONS.md hard rule 2 says a defect in an existing core primitive is fixed IN core, and the fix must ship a regression test in `packages/core/test/` that names the issue it closes. Core stays frozen to additions: add NO new export.

CONTEXT FOR THE BUILDER. Package `packages/core` (`@adlc/core`, one runtime dependency: `@adlc/tickets`): `lib/railpath.mjs` (32 lines: private `realpathOr(p)` + exported `resolveRailPath(filePath, root)`), re-exported by `index.mjs:13`, typed at `index.d.ts:323` (`(filePath: string, root: string): string`). Tests: `npm test -w packages/core` from the worktree root (runs `node --test test/*.test.mjs`, so a new file in `packages/core/test/` is picked up with no registry edit; the `pi` and `opencode` segments in `scripts/run-tests.mjs` are directory globs too). Importers: `plugins/adlc-opencode/rails-checker.mjs` (:12 import, :17 re-export, :616 use in `railHit`) and `plugins/adlc-pi/lib/rails-checker.mjs` (:13 import, :89 use in `railHit`); everything in those two plugins that decides a write goes through `railHit` (`plugins/adlc-opencode/index.mjs`, `plugins/adlc-opencode/lib/watcher.mjs`, `plugins/adlc-pi/lib/extension.mjs`, `plugins/adlc-pi/lib/gate-policy.mjs`). They resolve `@adlc/core` through the worktree's `node_modules/@adlc/core -> ../../packages/core` link created by `npm ci`, so their tests exercise THIS worktree's core only when `node_modules` is a real install, not a symlink to another checkout (`ls -ld node_modules` must show a directory). `plugins/adlc-cursor/rails-checker.mjs:139-161` and `plugins/adlc-gemini/rails-checker.mjs:208-230` are separate forked copies that already walk every level; they are NOT importers and are not part of this change. `railpath.mjs` is not a source in `scripts/ticket-readers/generate.mjs` ARTIFACTS, is not inlined in `plugins/adlc-gemini/*-inline.mjs`, and contributes zero bytes to the committed `plugins/adlc-cursor/bin/adlc-mcp-wrapper.bundle.mjs` (esbuild parses it but tree-shakes it, because the module has no top-level side effects) — nothing is regenerated or rebuilt by this change.

FIXTURE SHAPE (binding for all three new test files). `scripts/test/tmp-fixture-boundary.test.mjs` scans every `.mjs` under a `test/` directory and fails on a `mkdtempSync(` whose result is not bound DIRECTLY to a name and paired with a removal; `realpathSync(mkdtempSync(...))` is reported as a leak, and its ALLOWLIST may only shrink. Use exactly this shape:

    import { test, after } from 'node:test';
    const dirs = [];
    after(() => { for (const d of dirs) rmSync(d, { recursive: true, force: true }); });
    function makeRepo() {
      const dir = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'railpath-deep-'));
      dirs.push(dir);
      const root = realpathSync(dir);
      ...
      return root;
    }

Every additional `mkdtempSync` in these files (the second temp directory of the symlinked-root case in AC1) follows the same two lines: bind to a `const`, then `dirs.push(<name>)`. Do not add any file to that ALLOWLIST and do not edit `packages/core/test/railpath.test.mjs` (it is listed there and must stay byte-identical).

NORMATIVE BEHAVIOUR.
1. Algorithm of `resolveRailPath(filePath, root)`: `abs` = `filePath` if absolute, else `join(root, filePath)`. Starting at `cur = abs`, while `cur` does not exist (`existsSync`): take `parent = dirname(cur)`; if `parent === cur` stop (filesystem root reached, nothing exists); otherwise prepend `basename(cur)` to the missing tail and continue from `parent`. The result is `join(realpathOr(cur), ...tail)` made relative to `realpathOr(root)`, with backslashes converted to `/`. An existing target is the zero-iteration case of the same walk, so no separate `existsSync(abs)` branch is needed. This is the same walk the two forked copies already perform; on every input the result must equal theirs.
2. Unchanged contract: same name, signature, synchronous string return; never throws for string arguments (`realpathOr` keeps returning its input on error); a path with no symlinked existing ancestor comes back as its lexical root-relative form; a symlink loop or a dangling directory link counts as missing, so the walk passes over it and the result stays lexical. No new export, `index.mjs` and `index.d.ts` untouched, and NO top-level side effects in `railpath.mjs` — only imports and function declarations at module level (that is what keeps it out of the cursor bundle).
3. Cost: one `existsSync` per missing trailing segment, the same profile as the forked copies. Do NOT add a segment cap, a path-length shortcut or any other numeric bound: a numeric boundary is a mutant no portable test can kill, and the importers' tests assert only the decision on very long paths (`plugins/adlc-opencode/test/rails-checker.test.mjs`, test `r: narrowed ancestor matching stays linear on a hostile target path`, which must stay green unedited).
4. Comments: replace the header at `:1-6` with a statement of the contract — what the function maps (a tool-supplied path to the forward-slash, root-relative path a write would really land on), why (a symlink whose real target is a frozen rail must not pass a lexical check), and the fallback. Remove the history sentence ("First shipped inline in plugins/adlc-opencode/rails-checker.mjs; hoisted here so every integration adapter shares one implementation."). Keep ONE JSDoc block on the function; do not restate the contract twice. Comments describe behaviour only.
5. Documentation: none. `packages/core/README.md`, `docs/tools/core.md` and `apps/docs/content/docs/toolkit/core.mdx` do not mention this function, the integration pages already state the intended behaviour ("symlink-aware rail resolution"), and `CHANGELOG.md` is written only by release bumps.

ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA.
- AC1 New file `packages/core/test/railpath-deep-ancestor.test.mjs`, whose header comment names issue #1062; it imports `resolveRailPath` from `'../lib/railpath.mjs'`. Fixture: `test/` and `src/` exist, `test/a.test.mjs` exists, `src/alias -> ../test` (relative link). It asserts, each as its own test: `'src/alias/newdir/x.test.mjs'` -> `'test/newdir/x.test.mjs'`; `'src/alias/n1/n2/n3/x.test.mjs'` -> `'test/n1/n2/n3/x.test.mjs'` (tail order); `join(root, 'src/alias/newdir/x.test.mjs')` -> `'test/newdir/x.test.mjs'` (absolute input); `'src/alias/n1/n2/'` -> `'test/n1/n2'` (trailing slash); with `hop -> src/alias`, `'hop/newdir/x.test.mjs'` -> `'test/newdir/x.test.mjs'` (chained links); with a second temp dir holding `repo -> root`, `resolveRailPath('src/alias/newdir/x.test.mjs', <that link>)` -> `'test/newdir/x.test.mjs'` (symlinked root). All six fail before the fix and pass after it. verify: `node --test packages/core/test/railpath-deep-ancestor.test.mjs`
- AC2 Same file, guards that pass before and after: `'src/new/deeper/file.ts'` -> unchanged; with `loopA -> loopB` and `loopB -> loopA`, `'loopA/d/x.mjs'` -> `'loopA/d/x.mjs'` (test option `{ timeout: 5000 }`); an absolute path whose first segment does not exist, `join(sep, 'railpath-absent-' + process.pid, 'a', 'b.mjs')`, -> `relative(root, abs).split(sep).join('/')` (`{ timeout: 5000 }`; the walk ends at the first existing ancestor, here the filesystem root); `'test/a.test.mjs/child/x'` -> unchanged (a regular file as an ancestor does not throw). The file must NOT assert anything about a symlink whose own target file is absent, nor about a `..` segment that follows a symlink (see OUT OF SCOPE). verify: `node --test packages/core/test/railpath-deep-ancestor.test.mjs`
- AC3 New file `plugins/adlc-pi/test/railpath-new-subdir.test.mjs`: fixture as AC1, `ticket = { id: 'T1', title: 'T1 fixture', rails: ['test/**'], scope: [] }`; `checkStructuredWrite('src/alias/newdir/x.test.mjs', ticket, root)` and `checkStructuredWrite('src/alias/a/b/x.test.mjs', ticket, root)` have `decision === 'deny'` with `reason` matching `/rail/` (both are `'allow'` before the fix); control `checkStructuredWrite('src/newdir/ok.mjs', ticket, root).decision === 'allow'`. Import from `'../lib/rails-checker.mjs'`. verify: `node --test plugins/adlc-pi/test/railpath-new-subdir.test.mjs`
- AC4 New file `plugins/adlc-opencode/test/railpath-new-subdir.test.mjs`: temp repo with `.adlc/tickets.json` = `{"tickets":[{"id":"T1","title":"T1 fixture","rails":["locked/**"]}]}`, directory `locked/`, link `aliasdir -> <dir>/locked`, `env = { ADLC_P4_ENFORCEMENT: '1', ADLC_TICKET: 'T1' }` (pass `env` explicitly, never `process.env`); `checkRail({ filePath, tool: 'write', root: dir, env }).decision` is `'deny'` for `'aliasdir/newdir/new.mjs'` and `'aliasdir/a/b/new.mjs'` (both are `'allow'` before the fix), and `'allow'` for the control `'src/newdir/ok.mjs'`. Import from `'../rails-checker.mjs'`. verify: `node --test plugins/adlc-opencode/test/railpath-new-subdir.test.mjs`
- AC5 Existing suites green with no edits to them, including every importer test that reaches `railHit`. verify: `npm test -w packages/core`, `node --test plugins/adlc-pi/test/*.test.mjs` and `node --test plugins/adlc-opencode/test/*.test.mjs` (the `pi` and `opencode` segment commands of `scripts/run-tests.mjs`) all exit 0, and `git diff --exit-code --stat $(git merge-base origin/main HEAD) -- packages/core/test/railpath.test.mjs packages/core/index.mjs packages/core/index.d.ts packages/core/package.json scripts/test/tmp-fixture-boundary.test.mjs plugins/adlc-cursor plugins/adlc-gemini plugins/adlc-pi/lib plugins/adlc-opencode/rails-checker.mjs` exits 0 with no output
- AC6 Header states the contract, history removed. verify: `grep -c "First shipped inline\|hoisted here" packages/core/lib/railpath.mjs` prints `0` (it prints `2` before the change) and `grep -c "deepest existing ancestor" packages/core/lib/railpath.mjs` prints `1` or more (keep that phrase on one line)
- AC7 Repo-level guards unaffected. verify: `node --test scripts/test/tmp-fixture-boundary.test.mjs` exits 0; `node --test plugins/adlc-cursor/test/packaging.test.mjs` exits 0 WITHOUT running `npm run build:cursor-mcp` (if it is red, first check `ls -ld node_modules` is a real directory; otherwise `railpath.mjs` gained a top-level side effect — fix the module, do not rebuild the bundle); `node scripts/ticket-readers/generate.mjs --check` exits 0
- AC8 Mutation gate green on the branch. verify: `node scripts/mutation-gate.mjs origin/main --max 12` exits 0 (also run `--max 80` once locally before opening the PR)

OUT OF SCOPE: a symlink whose OWN target does not exist yet (`alias.mjs -> test/new.test.mjs` with the target file absent) still resolves lexically here and in both forked copies — it needs lstat/readlink handling and is a separate change; do not half-fix it and do not pin it in a test. The same goes for a `..` segment that follows a symlinked directory (`src/alias/../x`): `join` folds it lexically before any symlink is resolved, here and in both forked copies. The forked copies in `plugins/adlc-cursor/rails-checker.mjs` and `plugins/adlc-gemini/rails-checker.mjs` (and any de-duplication of them), `packages/core/lib/shell.mjs`, the `export { resolveRailPath }` re-export in the opencode checker, any change to `canonicalizePath`/`railHit` in the importers, Windows-specific symlink behaviour, and shrinking the fixture ALLOWLIST.
